   "notes": "10-15 Market Passage, south side of the lane, faces NORTH (Market Passage, not Market St). Victorian gault (buff) brick, three storeys, with red-brick round-arched heads to tall first-floor windows and red-brick heads/bands to the second floor; dark painted shopfronts and cafe units at ground level (fascias mostly blank). Six window columns estimated from raking views along the lane; positions spaced evenly."
